1
00:00:12,706 --> 00:00:13,746
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:45,973
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,093 --> 00:00:48,320
=Episode 20=

4
00:00:51,026 --> 00:00:52,453
(Guizhen Cottage)

5
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,479
(Xiao Che sees us)

6
00:00:54,759 --> 00:00:55,880
(as mere weeds. Our lives mean nothing.)

7
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:57,679
(A little kindness)

8
00:00:57,679 --> 00:00:59,159
(can buy our gratitude.)

9
00:00:59,159 --> 00:00:59,960
(Here's a prescription.)

10
00:01:00,759 --> 00:01:01,759
(What he doesn't know)

11
00:01:02,079 --> 00:01:03,119
(is every wrong they swallow,)

12
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:04,560
(every pain they bear,)

13
00:01:05,119 --> 00:01:07,119
(will come to me, one by one,)

14
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,520
(and in my hands)

15
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:11,120
(weave a net that claims their lives.)

16
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,920
We've gathered all the evidence
of the crimes at Guizhen Cottage.

17
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:28,959
Thank you.

18
00:01:30,519 --> 00:01:31,319
(Shouhe.)

19
00:01:32,359 --> 00:01:33,319
(Wait a little longer.)

20
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:35,560
(They owe you a life.)

21
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:38,760
(I'll make them pay, bit by bit.)

22
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:39,799
Take care.

23
00:01:41,239 --> 00:01:41,959
Your Highness.

24
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:44,879
Vice Director Shen wrote.

25
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,079
Chunya has been caught.

26
00:01:58,359 --> 00:01:59,599
Concubine Hui...

27
00:02:02,439 --> 00:02:03,400
She...

28
00:02:04,079 --> 00:02:06,159
She already knew Chunya
had drugged the wick.

29
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,159
Yet she still let His Majesty
have his way.

30
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:11,200
She used her own child to set a trap

31
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,959
just to frame me.

32
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:16,080
Your Highness, you mean...

33
00:02:17,039 --> 00:02:18,560
she caused her own miscarriage?

34
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:21,960
Even a tiger won't eat its own cubs.

35
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:25,360
Su Cao... How dare you...

36
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,199
Ruolan.

37
00:02:32,039 --> 00:02:32,879
Tell me.

38
00:02:34,759 --> 00:02:36,680
Could it be...

39
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,639
there was never a child to begin with?

40
00:02:46,879 --> 00:02:47,919
I hear the whole capital

41
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:50,800
is talking about Concubine Hui's clinic.

42
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:52,759
They praise Your Majesty

43
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,199
for virtue that moves Heaven,

44
00:02:54,719 --> 00:02:56,039
and Concubine Hui for her compassion.

45
00:02:56,599 --> 00:02:58,240
Even you, Imperial Uncle,
secluded in a Buddhist hall,

46
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,360
have heard about it.

47
00:03:01,319 --> 00:03:02,520
Her fame has spread far and wide.

48
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,039
There's no stopping it.

49
00:03:05,199 --> 00:03:07,479
Concubine Hui does have a kind heart.

50
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,439
Roujia's death anniversary is near.

51
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,960
She even asked permission

52
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:14,840
to set up a free clinic by the cottage.

53
00:03:15,719 --> 00:03:16,560
I approved it.

54
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,039
I'm sure Roujia

55
00:03:20,159 --> 00:03:21,599
would be pleased to know.

56
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,879
Wise choice, Your Majesty.

57
00:03:28,039 --> 00:03:28,840
(Roujia,)

58
00:03:30,039 --> 00:03:32,000
(a storm is finally brewing here.)

59
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,680
(I only wonder whether it will)

60
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,120
(sweep away the old injustices)

61
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,479
(or bring fresh bloodshed.)

62
00:03:43,639 --> 00:03:44,919
Everything here

63
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,759
was arranged just as Roujia had wished.

64
00:03:49,439 --> 00:03:50,719
She always said

65
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,599
we should live simply

66
00:03:53,319 --> 00:03:54,680
and share the people's hardships.

67
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:58,319
All these years,

68
00:03:59,039 --> 00:04:01,039
I've come here every year.

69
00:04:31,279 --> 00:04:32,360
(Almost done.)

70
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,319
(Finish it soon.)

71
00:04:35,279 --> 00:04:36,160
(Then I can get home sooner.)

72
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:37,920
(Wanniang is waiting for me.)

73
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:41,700
♪The cool night flows like water♪

74
00:04:42,813 --> 00:04:44,500
♪Jackdaws sigh♪

75
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:47,080
♪The moon sets over a lonely mountain♪

76
00:04:47,133 --> 00:04:50,040
♪The wind whips my worn, thin clothes♪

77
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:52,533
♪The road ahead is hard♪

78
00:04:53,346 --> 00:04:55,380
♪My heart drifts away with the clouds♪

79
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:58,800
♪Frost coats the old zither strings♪

80
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:03,200
♪My old home has stood empty ten years♪

81
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:07,080
♪Looking back, it all fades like smoke♪

82
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:10,346
♪No one by my side♪

83
00:05:11,226 --> 00:05:15,400
♪Life is a dream, shattered on waking♪

84
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:19,650
♪We're at opposite ends of the world♪

85
00:05:20,453 --> 00:05:24,420
♪A flute echoes by the broken bridge♪

86
00:05:24,786 --> 00:05:29,940
♪Years pass, my tears dry in the wind♪

87
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:30,800
What's wrong?

88
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:34,786
♪All in vain♪

89
00:05:40,399 --> 00:05:41,160
Nothing.

90
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:44,839
The craftsmanship is exquisite.

91
00:05:45,079 --> 00:05:46,720
I was captivated by it.

92
00:05:51,199 --> 00:05:52,160
Yes.

93
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:53,480
The craftsman...

94
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,800
was quite ingenious.

95
00:05:57,319 --> 00:05:58,959
What was his name again?

96
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,079
What a pity.

97
00:06:02,079 --> 00:06:03,160
His life was cut short.

98
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:06,360
He died in an accident
after finishing this screen.

99
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,279
Perhaps that's for the best.

100
00:06:09,959 --> 00:06:11,279
At least his talent

101
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,279
didn't go to waste.

102
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:21,160
His work remains here,

103
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:22,800
keeping Roujia company.

104
00:06:24,199 --> 00:06:25,560
That was a blessing for him.

105
00:06:27,079 --> 00:06:28,160
(A blessing?)

106
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,199
Su.

107
00:06:46,839 --> 00:06:49,000
Your Majesty,
you value his work so highly.

108
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,120
If he knew beyond the grave,

109
00:06:51,399 --> 00:06:52,360
I'm sure

110
00:06:54,319 --> 00:06:55,600
he'd be moved to tears with gratitude.

111
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:06,800
You look pale.

112
00:07:13,319 --> 00:07:15,000
I was moved

113
00:07:15,279 --> 00:07:16,959
by how deeply

114
00:07:17,399 --> 00:07:18,519
Your Majesty still loves

115
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:21,399
the late Empress.

116
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,720
I'd like to stay here

117
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,000
and light some incense for her

118
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,160
to pay my respects.

119
00:07:33,839 --> 00:07:34,480
All right.

120
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:35,959
Then I'll

121
00:07:36,639 --> 00:07:37,839
go check the herbal medicine stall.

122
00:08:01,649 --> 00:08:05,836
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

123
00:08:05,970 --> 00:08:09,583
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

124
00:08:09,818 --> 00:08:12,417
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

125
00:08:12,454 --> 00:08:14,734
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

126
00:08:14,781 --> 00:08:18,610
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

127
00:08:19,012 --> 00:08:22,365
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

128
00:08:23,292 --> 00:08:26,805
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

129
00:08:27,305 --> 00:08:29,872
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

130
00:08:29,998 --> 00:08:32,031
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

131
00:08:32,098 --> 00:08:35,875
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

132
00:08:36,225 --> 00:08:40,558
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

133
00:08:40,781 --> 00:08:44,288
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

134
00:08:44,469 --> 00:08:47,322
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

135
00:08:47,389 --> 00:08:53,003
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

136
00:08:53,043 --> 00:08:56,057
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

137
00:08:56,098 --> 00:09:02,106
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

138
00:09:02,773 --> 00:09:08,760
♪The past has faded away♪

139
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:13,760
♪The past has faded away♪
